      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1895-10-05_WidnesExaminer_art0022" n="art0022">
        <head>"NEW WOMAN'S COLONY."</head>
        <p>A "NEW WOMAN'S COLONY."</p>
        <p>- - - - - Dr. Mary Walker has just bought a farm of 135 acres near Oswego, in New York State, where she intends to found a colony for women only. Speaking of the scheme on Sunday, she said that all colonists would live in one commodious house, under the immediate supervision of herself and two elected lady officers. " Bloomers " will be compulsory. at Oswego. Applicants for membership will have to pledge them-elves to celibacy during their stay in the colony. Womsn above fifteen and under thirty-five, who are prepared to abjure flirting with out- siders and similar frivolities will be eligible. Themono- tony of farm life will be varied by the study of politics. of literature, and of social questiors, as well as by 1" manly " sports. The chief object of tbe scheme, ac- I cording to Dr. Walker is to educate and turn out credit- able specimens of the New Woman. The site selected is in the heart of the picturesque fruit country. Dr. Walker la confident that her farm will prove to be what ,he calls it—the Garden of Eden without Adam.</p>
        <p>Jewellery valued at nearly £l,OOO has been stolen by burglars trona a shop at Brighton.</p>
