        <p>Lot 1. Splendid house of ,Furniture, complete, the most substantial lot in this city, and containing more for the money. The Dining-room has a heavy Dining-room Suite, complete, in hard grain, Levant leather, the frames beauti- fully carved in has relief ; has comfortable couch andluxuri- ously upholstered easy chairs, a heavy dining table toe etch, extends to dine 10, with Incised early English legs n patent casters; a handsome Per lan bordered carpet and rug to match, solid brass bar fender,fire brasses and dogs complete; cornice, with rings, ends and brackets ; Notting am tace curtains ; and las:. width is thrown in gratis and is in addi- tion to what any competitor could do, simply for an adver- tisement, a handsome American walnut sideboard, in the Renaissance style. to match the dining-room suite. The Bedroom :Suite's solid Cypru, wood ant 4 is a suite which can be highly recommended, guaranteed for 10 years, being ' charged in some establishments as much a, we ask for the I whole of this house of furniture; a handsome solid brass and eatiq elled bedstead, with complete fittit.gs of mattress and bedding; there are the usual accessories for bedroom—carpets, curthins, fender, chamber ware. etc. Also Kitchen Furni- ture, consisting of the usual chairs, hsavy white top table, fender, ashcan, and top bar, floorcloth for kitchen, landing, and hall. I will pack and deliver the lot for 21i guineas, 10 per cent, extra if by defernd payments. Call and inspect this lot, it pulverises all competition ; if you approve buy, if you don't there is no harm done..—WORSLEY'S. Lot 2. A Splendid House of Furniture for £4O, solid oak and walnut, heavy massive furniture throughout, in capital condition, worth £BO, dining-room, two bedrooms, kitchen, hall stairs, and landing ; a great bargain. Lot 3. A workingman's House of Furniture for £l5 ; a splendid bargain. There is better stronger, and more furni- ture in this lot than many competitors offer for £3O. Lot 4. The best House of Furniture for £6O ever offered. Same quantity as Lot 2, but higher class, except that we are prepared, as an advertisement, to present a wanoforte with this lot or its value. This offer holds good for H days only. Lot 5. And last, but not least, we have a magnificent House of Furniture, deposited by the executors of a deceased gentleman. of Alderley, with us for immediate disposal. Price for the lot. £2OO. Contains superb furniture for draw- ing, &amp;fling. sitting. and three bedromps ; kitchen. hill, stairs, landing ; besides sundries ; honestly worth £5OO. Full and complete particulars on application.</p>
        <p>GREAT BARGAINS IN DINING-ROOM FURNIT URN LOT 113. A remarkably handsome carved oak Dining- room Suite, in morocco, hair stuffed, bold, massive, an haadsome ; couch, two easys. six chairs' six-feet sideboard. eight-feet dining fable, Sue bold overmantel, co,I caldnet, the lot complete for £45 ; worth £2OO. —WORSLEY'S. LOT 212. A capital solid American Walnut Dining-room Suite, in best English Moroco, hair stuffed throughout, the framework is h,-avy, magnikently carved in bas relief, consists of broad comfortab.e couch, pair of luxuriously up- -1 holsteredeasy chairs, a set of six high-padded back standard single chairs, all upholstered in a rich wine-coloured turkey grain Morocco, beautifully banded and studded, cost £7O ; price £l5 155., guaranteed for 10 years. The sideboard is of noke proportions, of modern design, well equipped with every modern convenience; early English design, fitted with broad deeply-cut bevelled edge mirrors of great lustre and brilliancy, cost £65, for 16 guineas. A massive handsome Dining Table, £3 10s. ' cast £l2 10s., and Overmantel, which matches the sideboard, for £6 10s.. worth £25. All the above in splendid conditi, n.—WORS</p>
        <p>Lot 251. A heavy handsomely-carved Dining Room Suite In Oriental saddle bags, a full snite of nine pieces, together with magnificent couch and easy chairs ; honestly worth £45, for 14 guineas.—Wi Lot 261. Excellent Spanish Mahogany and Morocco Dining Room Suite, nine pieces complete; cost £.50, for 8 guineas.— WORSLhY'S.</p>
        <p>Over 27,0 Dining-room Suites on view, from £2 to £500; over 200 Sideboards. from 355. to 100. guineas ; over 300 Dining Tables, from 15s. tu £2O; over 400 Overmantels. all shapes, styles, and sizes, from Bs. 6d. to £3O.—WORSLEY'S. inspection invited.</p>
