        <p>L0t759. High-class Second-hand Bedroom Suite,by Henry Ogden and bons, Spanish Mahogany, consisting of 7ft, Spanish mahogany wardrobe, rich in colour. modern fittings, worth £76, for £3O. Pair of the handsomest stands to match in Manchester; dressiug.table sft., washstand 411. 6in. for 18i guineas. worth £45. Lot 791, A grand Bedroom Suite by Todd. In American walnut richly and profusely carved in has relief ; a suite greatly admired. Wardrobe is a masterpiece of design and workmanship, beautifully finished inside with modern con- veniences, Dressing tab'e is mounted with largeswing bevel- led mirror and jewel drawers. Washstand fitted with Carrara marble slab and back, three chairs, towel rail, and table de unit complete, a very charming and effective suite ; price I only 18 guineas ; worth trebIe.—WOUSLRY'S. Lot 782. A similar Suite to Lot 791, same number of pieces for 10 guineas ; cost £35. WORSLRY'S. A wonderful bar- gain. Lot 793. A genuine Sheraton Bedroom Suite, 6ft. Bln.,cost £25(.), for £59 15s. ; a real gem, worth seeing, first come, first served.—WORSLEY'S. Lot 891. American Ash Bedroom Suite, cost £75, by Hud- son, £22. Similar to lot 863. Lot 897. Spanish Mahogany Wardrobe, break front, project- ing centre door, with full length crystal bevelled mirror, in ceingnstirine, twed, bonnet largeonne hangingtdrawer compartmentss,fourtraye, thinreethleowug long drawers handsome, for £l5 lbs. ; worth £5O.</p>
        <p>Lot 19.—Full-compaas Iron-frame Cottage, by Brinsmead, 25 15.. Lot 27.—Fu11-cumpass Iron-frame Cottage, by Collard, 11 £lO 105. Lot 35.—Fu11-compass Iron-frame Cottage, by Hopkinson, 5217 10s. Lot 47.—Fu11-compass Iron-frame Cottage, by Burling, 26 10s. Lot 49.—Fu11-compasl Iron-frame Cottage, by Erard, 218 18s. Lot 55.—Fine Handsome Cottage Pianoto le, by Bogg and Sons; the speciality Mau°, 7 octaves, Ato A. full trichmd ; advertised for 24 guineas; price 14 guineas ; a bargain. Lot 63.—Magnificent Iron-frame New Pianoforte, by the renowned maker Kirkman. London guaranteed for 20 years ; in rosewood; all latest Improvements; worth 60 guineas, music sellers' price ; our priee. 29 guineas. Lot 71.—Pine Steinway Model Upright Grand Cottsge Pianoforte, by Hilton and Hilt ; quite new ; splendid burr walnut case; a wonderful piano; highly recommended; gained the gold medal; pric, 28/ guineas ; worth 61 guineas. LOT 75.—Blegaut Burr Walnut Piano. by Collard and Col- lard, second-hand, but equal to new : cost 85 guineas ; a genuMe high-class instrument for £3l; money returned if no' satisfactory in every respects.—Worsley's. LOT 110.—A Powerful Full-tone Upright grand, by Collard and Collard, in rosewood; cost £65 ; for £24 10s. almost new. LOT 120 —Very Handsome Piano, by John Broadwood and and Sons, in solid rosewood; magnificent tone ; full compass, A to A ; cost 60 to 70 guineas • price £2l ; a bargain. I LOT 134.—0ne of the Finest Instruments ever made,by that noted maker Brard ; second-hand •, wonderful tone, beautful touch,repetitlon action,in splendid condition; for 27/ guineas; worth three times the money. LOT 137.—Handsome and Powerful-tone Pianoforte, up- right grand cottage, by Sehiedtnayer ; £35 ; worth £lOO ; new. LOT 141 —Magnificent Upright Grand Cottage, by J. and J. Hoplf inson, London ; cost £75 ; for 19 guineas. LOT 143.—Fu11-compass Iron-frame Cottage, by Brinsmead, 218. _</p>
        <p>Lot 145.—1r0n-frame Cottftge Piano, by Justin Browne, £2O. Lots 146 to 176 —Splendid Collection of Thirty Second hand Plane, by first-rate makers, from £1 10s. to £l6. cVe quote a few samples only: —Collard and Collard, 30s. ; Broad. wood, 505.: Balllngall, £4 10s.; Cadby, £6 106 ; Burling and Burling, £7 10s.; Locke and eons, £10; Ohallen, £l2; Chap- pell, £l4 • Bord. £l5. Worsley's. Fifty dagnificent New instruments, from £l2 to £5O. On view.</p>
        <p>LO 215.—Fine American Organ, by Green, full compass, in massive carved Ame,ican walnut ease; seven sets of reeds; full Bourdon reeds; a wonderful bargain; £l5 15s. ; worth £l5. Lot 217.—Splendid Harmonium, ful compsss, splendid Gone, in excellent condition, fk,r £3 158.; cost 18 guineas. Lot 225.—Magnificent American Organ, cost £3O, by Minion and Hamlin, for 10 guineas.</p>
