        <p>A B OOK FOR MARRIED WOMEN The information contained In this book ought to be known by every married woman, and it will cot harm the tuanarriep to read. The book is cmveniently divided into 12 ,chapters The first chapter treats of the changes at puberty, or when a girl becomes a woman. The second chapter treats of marriage from a doctor's standpoint ; points out the beat age for marriage, and who should have children and who not, and furnishes useful information that one can ordinarily get only from an intelligent doctor. The third chapter treats of the marriage of blood relations; and condemns such marriages as a rule. Chapter four treats of the signs of pregnancy. The fifth chapter tells how a woman should live during the pregnant state. Tne sixth chapter treats of mishaps and how to avoid them. The seventh chapter treats et maternal impressions and shows that birthmarks are not due be longings on the part ce the mother, but rather to her poor health. The eighth chapter teaches how to have easy confinement'. Certain people believe that women ghoul d bring forth in pain and trouble, but the hygienic physician says that confinement' can be made comparatively easy certain rules are obeyed ; those rules ere given. The ninth chapter treats of the proper management of confinement , until the baby is born. The tenth chapter tells how to treat he mother till she is up and about again. The eleventh chapter treats of sterility; gives the main causes of it, how . these may be overcome and children result. The last chapter treats of the "change." a most Important article for all women over forty. The book is full of useful information .and no book is written which goes so thoroughly into matters relating to married women. Some may think too much told ; such can scarcely be the ease. for knowledge is pews and the 1310111114 Of attaining happinesa. T e book can be he I rout Dr. T. B. ALLINSON, 25 Box. 4, 6panish-plaoe Manchester-square, London, W., in return for a Postal lirderle. Id. 474 TT OW TO ENSURE IIEALTII."—A medical JUL. work giving Prescriptions and Instructions for the Pure of all kinds of Debility : post free, two stampe.—A4dress Dr. Banana. 48, Lonsdale Square, Barnsbury, London. N.</p>
